# T-2484 — Charter canonical-sentence sync canary (G-019 charter-fork prevention)
# Source of truth: /opt/termlink/.context/cron/charter-sentence-drift-canary.crontab (git-tracked)
# Installed to:    /etc/cron.d/termlink-charter-sentence-drift-canary (USER field syntax — do NOT load into a user crontab)
#
# WHY: P1 (T-2470) shipped docs/CHARTER.md as "the single owned statement of what
# TermLink is". The canonical purpose sentence exists as THREE copies —
# docs/CHARTER.md (bold), README.md (plain), docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (blockquote) —
# and markdown has no transclusion, so editing one silently strands the other two.
# Nothing verified they stay identical: the charter, anchor of the whole T-2468 arc,
# was not load-bearing for its own consistency claim (G-019).
#
# This is the 13th canary (empty log = healthy). It extracts + normalizes the
# sentence from all three files and FIRES (exit 1, log entry) if they diverge.
# Sibling of the P8 charter-drift canary (T-2483): P8 guards the TOOL SURFACE
# against off-charter breadth; THIS guards the CHARTER SENTENCE against forking.
#
# Operator action on firing: docs/CHARTER.md is authoritative (human-blessed) — bring
# README.md + docs/ARCHITECTURE.md back into agreement with it. Ad-hoc check:
# `bash scripts/check-charter-sentence-drift.sh`. /canaries auto-discovers this log.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Daily at 09:07 UTC — offset from the 08:17/08:47 charter-drift (P8) neighbours.
7 9 * * * root cd /opt/termlink && bash scripts/check-charter-sentence-drift.sh --quiet >> .context/working/.charter-sentence-drift-canary.log 2>> .context/working/.charter-sentence-drift-canary.log.stderr

# Meta-canary (T-1723): a second daily run 30m later verifies THIS canary is still
# firing at all — the aliveness log grows when the heartbeat is stale (canary broke).
37 9 * * * root cd /opt/termlink && HEARTBEAT_FILE=.context/working/.charter-sentence-drift-canary.heartbeat CANARY_NAME="charter-sentence-drift canary" CANARY_PROBE_CMD="bash scripts/check-charter-sentence-drift.sh --quiet --no-heartbeat" CANARY_CRON_PATH=/etc/cron.d/termlink-charter-sentence-drift-canary bash scripts/check-canary-aliveness.sh --quiet >> .context/working/.canary-aliveness.log 2>> .context/working/.canary-aliveness.log.stderr
